{"skill":{"slug":"generate-excel","displayName":"Create an Excel (.xlsx) file containing formatted data."},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1773758384899,"changelog":"Excel Generator Skill 1.0.0 – Initial Release\n\n- Generate professional Excel (.xlsx) spreadsheets from user data, tables, or reports.\n- Supports rich cell formatting: bold, text color, background color, and alignment.\n- Auto-adjusts column widths for optimal readability.\n- Handles missing dependencies automatically during file creation.\n- Converts chat tables or structured requests into downloadable Excel files.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"generate_excel.py","size":5856,"sha256":"7087ded1f012d5d8f065492ce15dcb507603c468f49d3e954a8beaa4a42704be","contentType":null},{"path":"skill.md","size":2190,"sha256":"7d5eec736e825b946eef9dbf290efb7a3b70805452c1a0c8525dd7f0dacfdafc","contentType":null},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1898,"sha256":"008eb4ecedc8ea3949f2f06be4a6cf1d12c3f33c84d467f35b58a6405a82c1d5","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789187746447,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"bc7dc82c74abbff31d504d0bdb29ce50062e6c0284c8c9d82b4429618b240e4d","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/bc7dc82c74abbff31d504d0bdb29ce50062e6c0284c8c9d82b4429618b240e4d","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780086179965},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":68,"severity":"HIGH","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":7,"checkedAt":1789187746447},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This Excel generator appears to match its purpose, but it automatically installs code dependencies and can write or overwrite spreadsheet files in arbitrary writable locations without clear user control.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Writing an Excel file is purpose-aligned, but the filename is caller-controlled and only receives an .xlsx suffix check before wb.save, so it can create or overwrite writable spreadsheets outside an intended output directory.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The Python module automatically runs pip install openpyxl at import time if the dependency is missing, with no version pin, hash, approved index, or confirmation gate.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The usage instructions mostly require explicit Excel/spreadsheet generation intent, but the standalone trigger keywords are broad enough that a host should avoid activating it on ambiguous mentions.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"No backdoor, service, scheduled task, memory write, privilege escalation, or credential use was found, but the runtime dependency installation can persistently mutate the Python environment.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The skill coherently creates formatted .xlsx spreadsheets from user-provided tabular data using openpyxl; no unrelated credential access, exfiltration, destructive logic, or prompt hijacking was found.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Review this skill before installing in a shared or sensitive agent environment. Prefer running it only in a sandboxed workspace with no valuable spreadsheet files in writable paths, preinstall a pinned openpyxl dependency through your normal package process, and require explicit user confirmation for output filenames and overwrites. Treat workbook cell values from untrusted sources carefully because formula-like strings may remain active in the generated spreadsheet.","findings":"[SDI-2] expected: Verified: the skill discloses automatic dependency handling and the script installs openpyxl when missing, but doing this automatically at runtime is under-scoped for a spreadsheet generator.\n[AST3] expected: Verified but downgraded: __import__ is used only inside a helper with a fixed openpyxl call in this artifact, not to load arbitrary user-selected modules.\n[AST4] expected: Verified: subprocess executes python -m pip install openpyxl automatically, creating supply-chain and environment-mutation risk despite the fixed package name.\n[OH3] expected: Downgraded: the cited max_length value is part of column-width calculation and width is capped at 50; the artifact does not show log flooding or prompt-output stuffing behavior.\n[SQP-2] expected: Verified: file generation is expected, but the output path is not confined and existing files are not checked before saving.\n[SQP-1] expected: Partly accepted: the intent section is specific, but generic trigger keywords such as Excel and Spreadsheet could cause over-activation if the host treats them literally.\n[SQP-3] expected: Downgraded: bilingual trigger terms match the Chinese comments and examples in the artifact and are not independently suspicious.\n[T08] expected: Accepted: the unpinned import-time pip installation is artifact-backed and is the main install-mechanism concern.\n[T09] expected: Accepted in part: unrestricted output paths and possible spreadsheet formula injection are real risks when data or filenames are untrusted, though they are bounded to generated .xlsx files and do not show malicious intent.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789187746447}}}}}